WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.768
-Welcome to "Late Night."
Today, the president

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:05.104
reeled off an unhinged rant
in a call with governors,

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:08.307
demanding that they dominate
protesters with mass arrests

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:10.844
after days of violent police
escalation and unrest

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.111
over the murder of George Floyd.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:14.647
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:18.751
♪♪

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:21.487
-President Trump has been
quietly hunkered down

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:24.390
in the White House, occasionally
threatening wild fantasies

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.927
of violence against protesters
and belching out random

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.895
all-caps tweets, like,
"FAKE NEWS!"

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:31.197
And "LAW AND ORDER!"

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.032
We're in the middle
of a national crisis,

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.900
and he tweets like he's yelling
at his Roku

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.102
to change the channel.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.670
[ As Trump ] Law and order!

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.840
Below deck! Playboy Channel!

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:46.812
Uh, Mnuchin, we need to pay
for the Playboy Channel.

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:48.114
[ Normal voice ] And then today,
Trump reeled off

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.916
a deranged screed in a call
with governors

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.951
where he sounded like a cross

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.153
between a brutal military
dictator

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.489
and a racist grandpa shuffling
around the nursing home

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.057
with his robe on backwards.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.992
-President Trump today
venting frustration

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:01.193
at some of the nation's
governors.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.295
In a conference call,

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.429
the president
was at the White House.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.231
The president calling governors
"weak,"

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:08.001
saying they need a more robust
police response

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.236
to the protests going on now
across the country.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.872
-President Trump is criticizing
the nation's governors

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:17.109
for being "fools" in their
response to violent protests.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:19.945
The "Associated Press"
quotes Trump as saying,

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:21.414
"Most of you are weak.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.984
You have to arrest people and
put them in jail for 10 years

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.654
and you'll never see this stuff
again."

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:30.089
-He said, "You have to dominate.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.692
If you don't dominate,
you're wasting your time.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.194
They're going to run over you.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.828
You're going to look like
a bunch of jerks.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.730
You have to dominate."

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.699
-They look like jerks?

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.867
You're the one who's been
cowering in the White House

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:42.735
with the lights off.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.003
I mean, look at that.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.338
That's our White House.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.473
Right now, Donald Trump is going
from room to room

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.041
telling people to act like
they're not home

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.110
if the doorbell rings.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.210
[ As Trump ]
Nobody answer the door.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.012
I'm two weeks behind
on the rent.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.247
We used the money
for the Playboy Channel.

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:56.782
[ Normal voice ] The White House
has turned into the weird

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.951
abandoned house at the end of
the neighborhood the kids

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.954
dare each other to break into
on Halloween.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.455
"They say old man Trump still
lives up there in the attic

00:02:03.455 --> 00:02:04.590
with a corpse!"

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.859
"I'm not a corpse,
Mr. President."

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.628
[ As Trump ] Shut up, corpse,
they'll hear you!

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.664
If you had any doubts at all
about the dangers

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.467
of our overly militarized
police culture,

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.735
those doubts were answered.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.003
In the response
to the nationwide protests

00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:20.539
over the murder of George Floyd,
over the last few days,

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:23.309
we've all seen numerous examples
of police

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:26.378
being needlessly violent
or escalating their encounters

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:29.715
with protesters and reporters
for no legitimate purpose.

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:32.718
Like the many scenes of police
violently shoving people

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:36.022
to the ground or the police SUV
that drove into a crowd

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.790
in New York, or the officer
in Louisville

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.927
who just casually launched
what appeared to be pepper balls

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.896
at a local TV reporter covering
the scene from a distance.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.565
The police can't even get
through protests

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.334
against police brutality

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.269
without committing
more police brutality.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.771
It's like if your wife
accused you of having an affair

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:54.807
in divorce court, and you tried
to smooth it over

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.275
by seducing the judge.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:57.577
"Look, the only question I have,
your honor,

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:59.411
is what's under that robe?"

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:02.181
Even just showing up to
a protest in riot gear

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:05.818
with military equipment
is a form of escalation,

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.653
which we saw in cities
across the country,

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:10.356
like, for example,
in Columbia, South Carolina.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.993
Ask yourself, why do local
police departments have tanks

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.829
when doctors and nurses
can't even get masks and gowns?

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.232
We spend billions on military
equipment for police

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.734
and healthcare workers
have to wear snorkel masks

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.070
like retirees on vacation
in the Caribbean.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:27.306
There are teachers in this
country who are drowning in debt

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.774
and have to spend
their own money

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:30.176
to buy supplies
for their classrooms.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.344
If anyone deserves a tank,
it's them.

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.079
If you pulled up to your
high school and saw a tank

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:35.548
parked in the math teacher's
spot,

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.817
you'd learn what
a [bleep] fractal is.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.787
I still don't know,
'cause mine drove a Subaru.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.055
And in some cases,
the police excuses

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.756
for aggressively escalating
the violence

00:03:44.756 --> 00:03:46.025
have just been in absurd.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.260
Like in Louisville,
where police fired tear gas

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.163
at a peaceful protest
and claimed that it was

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:53.198
because police saw people
approaching

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:56.002
that had leaf-blowers
loaded with bleach

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.870
that was intended
to blow at police,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.738
so they sent out the tear gas.

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:01.140
First of all, in their defense,

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.175
they may have just heard
the president speak

00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:05.077
and then loaded up their
leaf-blowers with bleach

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.378
to cure corona.

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:08.080
"Open your mouths, everybody,
the worst is over!"

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.481
Vrrrrrrrrrrrrr!

00:04:09.481 --> 00:04:11.917
And second, a leaf-blower
loaded with bleach

00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:13.953
sounds like something
Kevin McCallister would use

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.054
against Harry and Marv.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.989
Were you also afraid
the protesters

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.692
would use a barbecue starter
to heat up a doorknob

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.661
or drop a tarantula
onto your face?

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.831
Even elected officials were not
immune from police violence,

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:27.833
as a New York state
assemblywoman, Diana Richardson,

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.902
explained after getting
pepper-sprayed

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.337
at a protest in Brooklyn.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:34.240
-The NYPD is being excessively
aggressive

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.177
with this crowd here,
and it is inappropriate!

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.646
I'm Assemblywoman
Diana Richardson.

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:42.147
I'm an elected official,

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:45.818
and they just pepper-sprayed me
for no reason!

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:48.588
And if anyone knows the law,
trust me, I know it.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.990
We were only peacefully
assembling.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.792
-You know, if you're going
to pepper spray

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.994
a group of peaceful protesters
unprovoked,

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:57.096
you might want to make sure
those protesters don't know

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.464
more about the law than you do.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:01.033
It's like trying to sell a
reverse mortgage to Tom Selleck.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.135
[ As Selleck ]
Nice try, those are just a trick

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:04.002
to take your house.

00:05:04.002 --> 00:05:05.404
Or like trying to sell

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:06.839
a used car to Dom Toretto.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:09.908
"Trust me, the Dodge Dart,
fastest car on the market."

00:05:09.908 --> 00:05:13.545
[ As Toretto ] It's not about
speed. It's about family."

00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:15.915
Did not use a second
of my week off

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.216
to work on my Vin Diesel
impression.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.350
The police, like the rest of us,

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.087
are supposed to be governed
by civilians

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.488
through a democratic process.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.624
They should never be seen
as above the process

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:27.326
because then that means
they're above accountability.

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:30.262
Civilian political leadership
are supposed to exercise

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:32.331
authority over the police
and hold them accountable

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:35.368
for abuses of power, just like
they would anyone else.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.703
Yet as we've seen in
New York City just this weekend,

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:38.971
too many of our leaders

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.140
have simply acquiesced
that authority.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.342
-New York City Police
are investigating this video

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:46.679
showing an NYPD cruiser ram into
a crowd during a protest.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.981
You can see the cruiser
behind a barrier

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:52.418
shortly after protesters began
throwing objects on Saturday.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.587
The cruisers
sort of lurches forward.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:56.355
No word yet on any injuries.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:59.392
New York mayor Bill de Blasio
refused to blame the officers,

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:01.327
saying he found the video
troubling,

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.962
but the protesters
did the wrong thing

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:06.031
to surround that police vehicle
and threaten the officers.

00:06:06.031 --> 00:06:09.067
-I saw a lot of restraint

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:11.337
under very, very difficult
circumstances.

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:14.006
Clearly, we need to do
a full investigation

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.142
and look at the actions
of those officers

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:18.544
and see what was done
and why it was done

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:19.979
and what could be done
differently.

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:22.815
I don't ever want to see a
police officer do that, period.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:24.183
Period. Ever.

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.319
But I also know that there was

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:28.454
an extremely dangerous
situation,

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.455
and the one thing they couldn't
do was stay there.

00:06:30.455 --> 00:06:31.590
-They could have just reversed.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:33.092
I mean,
they should know how to drive.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.361
They're cops, not Billy Joel.
If you don't get that joke,

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:36.829
don't worry, it just means
you're under 50.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.563
Congratulations on your youth.

00:06:38.563 --> 00:06:40.967
I know de Blasio doesn't drive
because he's so tall,

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:42.702
his head would
stick out of the sunroof.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:45.704
But he should know that cars
can go forwards and backwards.

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:48.207
So the police have cracked down
with impunity

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:50.008
on protests across the country.

00:06:50.008 --> 00:06:53.679
And yet, for a few soulless,
right-wing cable news husks,

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.047
that's not enough.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.516
-When you express an opinion
our leaders don't like,

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:58.985
they call it violence!

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:01.854
When criminals commit
actual acts of violence,

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.255
they call it speech.

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:04.991
So, the game is rigged.

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:07.760
Why are the rest of us
still playing it?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.828
None of the thugs looting Target

00:07:09.828 --> 00:07:11.964
or the well-paid nihilists
on television

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.934
who are egging them on
have added a thing. Nothing.

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:18.404
Should you keep playing along
with all of that?

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:22.308
Ponder that the next time
they demand you get a permit

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:24.510
to put a deck on your own house.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.047
-We all saw a man get murdered
by police

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:30.316
while begging for his life,
and your biggest concern

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:31.784
is putting a deck on your house?

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:33.085
Are you an actual person

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.922
or just a monogrammed towel
come to life?

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:37.490
We're in the middle
of an economic crisis

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.991
that has put 40-million people
out of work.

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:40.859
And this human penny loafer

00:07:40.859 --> 00:07:43.029
thinks the average American's
biggest concern right now

00:07:43.029 --> 00:07:44.763
is whether to go with redwood
or cedar.

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:48.734
Of course, it makes sense since
Mr. Faux Populism over here

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.670
always looks like the waiter
at his country club

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.872
just told him they were out
of foie gras.

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:56.409
But sadly, he's not alone.

00:07:56.409 --> 00:07:58.477
The president has repeatedly
threatened violence,

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:00.579
called for governors
to dominate protesters,

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:02.013
and insisted on law and order.

00:08:02.013 --> 00:08:04.250
But in reality,
the kind of order

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.018
people like Trump
or Tucker revere

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:07.619
is an order that only serves
them.

00:08:07.619 --> 00:08:09.722
They insist
that communities of color

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:12.858
politely and obediently
request change

00:08:12.858 --> 00:08:16.495
from a system that systemically
ignores, dehumanizes,

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:17.930
and disenfranchises them.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.265
We saw that on display
yet again this week

00:08:20.265 --> 00:08:22.601
with the rampant acts
of police escalation.

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:24.670
And we know it's not necessary,

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.305
because just a few weeks ago,

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:27.874
police were physically
confronted

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:30.843
by angry right-wing protesters
calling for an end to lockdowns.

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:32.911
And oddly, they seemed to have

00:08:32.911 --> 00:08:34.680
left their tanks
and tear gas at home.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.481
Man, I haven't seen white people
that angry

00:08:36.481 --> 00:08:38.016
since "Frasier"
went off the air.

00:08:38.016 --> 00:08:39.251
Granted,
different white people.

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:41.387
This was more
of a "Storage Wars" crowd.

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:44.257
And yet, in contrast to the
restraint police showed there,

00:08:44.257 --> 00:08:47.392
we have seen one video after
another over the last few days

00:08:47.392 --> 00:08:49.862
in which police needlessly
escalated encounters

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:52.130
with protesters, reporters,
and bystanders

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:53.833
for no legitimate purpose.

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:56.435
And in the face of that,
the very least we can do,

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.603
the absolute minimum
is to acknowledge

00:08:58.603 --> 00:09:01.540
that there is a deeply rooted
systemic problem here.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.877
We can't just gloss over it
with the same old excuses.

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:07.579
For example, we have to stop
saying [bleep] like this.

00:09:07.579 --> 00:09:11.250
-George Floyd is hardly
the only unarmed black American

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.652
killed recently by police.

00:09:12.652 --> 00:09:14.386
Do you think systemic racism

00:09:14.386 --> 00:09:16.989
is a problem in law enforcement
agencies in the United States?

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:19.391
-No, I don't think
there's systemic racism.

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:22.761
I think 99.9% of our
law enforcement officers

00:09:22.761 --> 00:09:24.363
are great Americans.
But you know what?

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:25.998
There are some bad apples
in there.

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:29.101
Because there's a few bad apples
that are giving law enforcement

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:30.969
a terrible name,

00:09:30.969 --> 00:09:33.605
and there's no doubt that
there's some racist police.

00:09:33.605 --> 00:09:34.807
I think they're the minority.

00:09:34.807 --> 00:09:36.409
I think they're
the few bad apples.

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:39.878
-Stop saying the problem
is just a few bad apples.

00:09:39.878 --> 00:09:42.348
It's not an apple problem.
It's an orchard problem.

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:44.516
If you went apple picking
and the guy who ran the orchard

00:09:44.516 --> 00:09:46.518
said "There are a few bad apples
out there."

00:09:46.518 --> 00:09:48.987
And you asked, "How bad?"
And they said, "Kill you bad."

00:09:48.987 --> 00:09:51.656
You'd say,
"This is a bad orchard."

00:09:51.656 --> 00:09:54.093
And now is not the time
to complain about it,

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:56.028
but apple picking [bleep] sucks.

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:57.463
Let's just all agree on that.

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:59.532
Why are apples the only food

00:09:59.532 --> 00:10:00.966
people want to pick
for themselves?

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:03.002
They all look the same.
And it's not even a challenge.

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:04.337
They're just dangling there.

00:10:04.337 --> 00:10:05.470
You know what would be
more exciting?

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:06.972
Catching your own turkey.

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:09.375
Then the best part about coming
home for Thanksgiving would be

00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:11.576
your mom serving, I don't know,
Thanksgiving spaghetti

00:10:11.576 --> 00:10:13.945
while your dad mutters
about his busted ankle.

00:10:13.945 --> 00:10:16.882
"They're faster than you think.
Tell you that much.

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:20.853
They look slow, but they --
they move."

00:10:20.853 --> 00:10:23.889
Putting it on a few bad apples
ignores the reality

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:25.324
that there's a predatory system

00:10:25.324 --> 00:10:27.192
with a history
of police misconduct

00:10:27.192 --> 00:10:29.661
built on a legacy of racism
and exploitation

00:10:29.661 --> 00:10:33.132
that elevates the comfort
and security of white people

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:34.667
over the health and safety
of black people.

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:39.038
This -- This is why we can't
just settle for mild reforms.

00:10:39.038 --> 00:10:41.340
Yes, we must demand
accountability,

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.808
but we can't stop there.

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:44.409
We need systemic change,

00:10:44.409 --> 00:10:46.311
and that extends to everything
from healthcare

00:10:46.311 --> 00:10:48.014
to housing to poverty.

00:10:48.014 --> 00:10:51.816
Just look at how our emphasis on
policing skews our priorities.

00:10:51.816 --> 00:10:54.086
New York City, for example,
spends more on policing

00:10:54.086 --> 00:10:56.889
than it does on the departments
of health, homeless services,

00:10:56.889 --> 00:10:58.657
housing preservation
and development,

00:10:58.657 --> 00:11:01.727
and youth and community
development combined.

00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:04.362
New York spends all that money
on police,

00:11:04.362 --> 00:11:07.032
and yet, apparently, their cars
don't even come with reverse.

00:11:07.032 --> 00:11:09.067
They should get a tip from

00:11:09.067 --> 00:11:11.202
[ As Vin Diesel ]
me, Vin Diesel.

00:11:11.202 --> 00:11:13.072
Now, see? It's getting --

00:11:13.072 --> 00:11:16.041
Maybe New York could start
to put some of that money aside

00:11:16.041 --> 00:11:18.210
for things like healthcare,
housing,

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:20.245
and signs at the top
of escalators

00:11:20.245 --> 00:11:21.747
that tell tourists,
"Do not stand here."

00:11:21.747 --> 00:11:24.750
I mean, that sign alone could
prevent 100 assaults a year.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.687
As a society, we spend more
on the systems

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:29.855
that punish and devalue
black lives

00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:32.557
than we do on the things that
reaffirm and empower black lives

00:11:32.557 --> 00:11:36.728
and allow people to live lives
of safety, decency, and health.

00:11:36.728 --> 00:11:39.565
We have to invest in things
like housing and healthcare.

00:11:39.565 --> 00:11:41.833
And we need laws restricting
the use of force,

00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:43.535
demilitarizing the police,

00:11:43.535 --> 00:11:46.172
and investing in nonviolent
alternatives to the police.

00:11:46.172 --> 00:11:48.006
We know these policies can work.

00:11:48.006 --> 00:11:49.741
We just need leaders
who will talk about them

00:11:49.741 --> 00:11:52.845
and who will talk about the ways
we can begin to dismantle

00:11:52.845 --> 00:11:55.881
the interlocking systems
of racism and injustice

00:11:55.881 --> 00:11:57.717
that perpetuate police violence.

00:11:57.717 --> 00:11:59.752
Instead, our president
has been cowering

00:11:59.752 --> 00:12:01.586
in the White House
with the lights off.

00:12:01.586 --> 00:12:05.057
100,000 Americans have died
in a public health crisis

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:07.693
that has disproportionately
preyed on communities of color.

00:12:07.693 --> 00:12:09.394
40-million people have lost
their jobs

00:12:09.394 --> 00:12:11.430
in an economic collapse
that has ravaged the poor

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:12.531
and working class.

00:12:12.531 --> 00:12:14.299
The murder of yet another
unarmed black man

00:12:14.299 --> 00:12:16.368
at the hands of police
has sparked a level of unrest

00:12:16.368 --> 00:12:18.270
this country hasn't seen
in our lifetimes.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:20.538
And the lights were off
at the White House.

00:12:20.538 --> 00:12:23.242
But honestly, I would take that
over Trump talking.

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:24.677
I mean,
what could he possibly say?

00:12:24.677 --> 00:12:26.078
We all know where he stands.

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:29.115
He praised Nazis and armed
white protesters in Michigan

00:12:29.115 --> 00:12:31.416
while denouncing black people
as thugs,

00:12:31.416 --> 00:12:34.019
threatening them with vicious
dogs and ominous weapons,

00:12:34.019 --> 00:12:37.055
and quoting a racist
police chief from the 1960s,

00:12:37.055 --> 00:12:38.390
which, by the way,
is just insane.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.826
The guy can't spell his wife's
name or his own name,

00:12:40.826 --> 00:12:42.294
but when it comes
to racist slogans,

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:44.263
he's like Little Man Tate.

00:12:44.263 --> 00:12:47.332
That one is for anyone
who's over 40.

00:12:47.332 --> 00:12:49.234
So, if you've got one,
if you got Little Man Tate,

00:12:49.234 --> 00:12:51.803
but not Billy Joel,
you're in your 40s.

00:12:51.803 --> 00:12:54.473
It's impossible to think
of a worse person

00:12:54.473 --> 00:12:57.009
to inhabit the most powerful
office in the country right now.

00:12:57.009 --> 00:12:58.910
Trump has been hiding away
in the White House

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:00.779
tweeting out wild fantasies
of violence,

00:13:00.779 --> 00:13:03.081
telling governors
to dominate protesters,

00:13:03.081 --> 00:13:05.183
and declaring,
without any apparent

00:13:05.183 --> 00:13:08.587
constitutional authority,
that he's designating Antifa,

00:13:08.587 --> 00:13:11.323
which isn't even a formal group,
a terrorist organization.

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:12.558
There's a good chance
he doesn't even know

00:13:12.558 --> 00:13:13.859
it stands for "antifascist."

00:13:13.859 --> 00:13:15.227
He probably thinks
it's a person.

00:13:15.227 --> 00:13:17.295
[ As Trump ]
Aunt Ifa, terrorist,

00:13:17.295 --> 00:13:20.566
and I'm not too fond of her
husband, Uncle Ifa, either.

00:13:20.566 --> 00:13:22.667
[ Normal voice ] So, you'd be
forgiven for watching all this

00:13:22.667 --> 00:13:25.370
and thinking that something
fundamental in America is broken

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:27.740
and that it's been broken
for a long time.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.908
Or as Cornel West put it...

00:13:29.908 --> 00:13:33.445
-We are witnessing America

00:13:33.445 --> 00:13:37.115
as a failed social experiment.

00:13:37.115 --> 00:13:40.719
What I mean by that is that
the history of black people

00:13:40.719 --> 00:13:43.188
for over 200 some years
and in America

00:13:43.188 --> 00:13:46.324
has been looking at America's
failure.

00:13:46.324 --> 00:13:49.961
Its capitalist economy
could not generate

00:13:49.961 --> 00:13:51.696
and deliver in such a way

00:13:51.696 --> 00:13:53.465
that people could live lives
of decency.

00:13:53.465 --> 00:13:56.468
The nation state,
its criminal justice system,

00:13:56.468 --> 00:13:59.438
its legal system could not
generate protection

00:13:59.438 --> 00:14:01.473
of rights and liberties.

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:03.708
But the question is,
we must fight,

00:14:03.708 --> 00:14:07.913
even in a moment in which we
have a failed social experiment.

00:14:07.913 --> 00:14:09.814
-Speaking of failed experiments,
our president

00:14:09.814 --> 00:14:12.451
looks like something from
a 1980s teen movie

00:14:12.451 --> 00:14:15.120
where two high schoolers
attach electrodes to a potato

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.422
and a confederate flag
to make him come to life.

00:14:17.422 --> 00:14:20.325
But even in the face of failure,
we have to keep fighting.

00:14:20.325 --> 00:14:23.562
We have to reaffirm every day
that black lives matter.

00:14:23.562 --> 00:14:26.765
And we have to work to dismantle
the interconnected systems

00:14:26.765 --> 00:14:28.533
of racism and injustice

00:14:28.533 --> 00:14:31.303
that devalue and disenfranchise
those lives.

00:14:31.303 --> 00:14:32.938
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:32.938 --> 00:14:36.075
♪♪

00:14:36.075 --> 00:14:38.710
Now more than ever, City Harvest
has been stepping up

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.445
to rescue and deliver more food

00:14:40.445 --> 00:14:42.414
to meet the increased need
in New York City.

00:14:42.414 --> 00:14:45.250
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:47.920
Stay safe, wash your hands,
we love you.

